      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Ordinary thiolate (RS-) reacts with diiodine (I2) to afford an intermediate sulfenyl iodide (RSI) by releasing I-; RSI is readily converted to disulfide (RSSR) by a disproportionation reaction. In the case of thiolate Ar1S- containing very bulky acylamino groups forming NH···S hydrogen bonds, the crystal of the intermediate, [Ar1S-I-I]-, was obtained under usual conditions, and the structure was determined by X-ray diffraction analysis. The results show that the intramolecular NH···S hydrogen bonds stabilized the intermediate [Ar1S-I-I]-, consistent with theoretical calculations."},
